    global_sffi_ratchets_drift_and_expose_unhardened_families_2026-08-26, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep2-20261127: reproduced both guard states. Classification with exact before/after: (1) outer raw-sffi-unsafe ratchet drift is REAL source drift (identity scheme verified unchanged; new rows are ABI changes like rt_get_args() -> [text] to -> [text]?; 4,105 new / 5,607 stale identities since the last baseline regen) - regenerating the baseline is explicitly banned by doc/08_tracking/bug/sffi_contract_inventory_red_on_origin_main_2026-09-03.md and hand-reviewing ~9.7k rows is the audit lane three prior triages deferred - left honest-red. (2) inventory ceilings 450/399 and 3950/3546 are real debt - ceilings not raised per doc. (3) the doc-named NULL-guard UDP family was the only remaining raw rt_io_udp_recv_from -> [u8] / -> i64 nonblocking-ABI surface repo-wide: both bench_udp_echo.spl copies (test/05_perf + test/perf, kept byte-identical) migrated to the checked ([u8], text)? / bool UDP ABIs with canonical @unsafe tags, unsafe(capabilities: [ffi]) scopes, recv size 65535 (65536 is rejected by the C provider guard); sffi-null-signature-guard findings 367 to 349 (all 18 UDP findings cleared); baseline pruned 8 rows with owner-note comments (wave-5 convention) reconciling current/new/stale exactly. (4) the doc-named crypto family deliberately NOT changed: ecdsa_p256 et al are identical on origin/main; the 2026-11-27 Batch-1 restoration wave explicitly kept caller-compatible [u8]/bool signatures with verified _checked variants - making sign_fixed return Result to satisfy the guard would undo that verified reconciliation (SFFI-authority-lane decision). Remaining ~349 findings are pre-existing cross-family debt red on origin/main too. Verification textual (two guards + ratchet selftest PASS + exact deltas): the lane seed predates the tree so the benches could not execute; they use the same r.0-projection idiom as the committed optional_tuple_byte_array_slot_spec (the regression test for that lowering), which carries the runtime confidence. Residual: baseline regen + crypto rename + TCP scoping etc remain with the SFFI authority lane per the doc. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/mir/optional_tuple_byte_array_slot_spec.spl prevention=test/perf/bench/http_server/bench_udp_echo.spl"

